From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: V <61495413+kelo221@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 11:59:14 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] calcActiveVoices_internal: map resample buffers when
 must-live voices fill the cap

When INAUDIBLE_TICK voices alone filled mMaxActiveVoices, the function
returned before mapResampleBuffers_internal, so active voices were mixed
with null mResampleData and the audio thread crashed.

Fixes upstream #279 (also reported as #205 and #327).
---
 src/core/soloud.cpp | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/core/soloud.cpp b/src/core/soloud.cpp
index e254457..872c264 100644
--- a/src/core/soloud.cpp
+++ b/src/core/soloud.cpp
@@ -2007,6 +2007,8 @@ namespace SoLoud
 			// ate all our active voice slots.
 			// This is a potentially an error situation, but we have no way to report
 			// error from here. And asserting could be bad, too.
+			// The active voices still need resample buffers before they are mixed.
+			mapResampleBuffers_internal();
 			return;
 		}
 
